{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2017-811", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2017/811", "wordCount": 2127, "segments": [{"start": 22.0, "text": "From first launch to your"}, {"start": 23.0, "text": "tutorial through your user"}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "interface, there's a lot that"}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "people experience in addition to"}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "your game's gameplay."}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "So, in the next few minutes, I'm"}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "going to cover 10 design tips to"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "create great experiences as soon"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "as someone taps your app icon."}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "And many of these tips can be"}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "applied to apps that are looking"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "to be just as immersive,"}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "engaging, and fun."}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "So, let's start."}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "First up is first Launch."}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "This is the first experience"}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "people have with your game and"}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "your first impression matters."}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "So, no matter what you need to"}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "say first, whether it is Accept"}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "Terms, or Headsets Recommended,"}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "design the first screen to fit"}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "within the style of your game."}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "That way, they're immersed"}, {"start": 65.0, "text": "immediately."}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "This edge to edge illustration"}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "from Pokemon Go does a great"}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "job, and it communicates just as"}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "much as the text on screen."}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "So, take the time to design what"}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "people see first as soon as they"}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "launch your game."}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "When this is done well, it'll"}, {"start": 81.0, "text": "make a lasting impression and"}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "set the tone for the rest of"}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "your game."}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "Next, is Loading because"}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "sometimes it takes just a few"}, {"start": 89.0, "text": "seconds to pull data through"}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "space."}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "So, why not take advantage of"}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "what we all know to be true,"}, {"start": 95.0, "text": "time flies when you're having"}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "fun."}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "So, during Loading, make it fun"}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "by educating or entertaining;"}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "then, Loading won't see to take"}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "as long."}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "This is Don't Starve Pocket"}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "Edition, and in this game"}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "Loading is masked by this"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "beautifully creepy animation,"}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "players are entertained, and"}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "time seems to fly by."}, {"start": 118.0, "text": "Loading is also a great time to"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "educate."}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "In Clash Royale, as you prepare"}, {"start": 123.0, "text": "for battle, a gameplay tip is"}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "shown on screen."}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "Now, if you choose to do this,"}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "make sure that players have"}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "enough time to read the tip and"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "also be intelligent about what"}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "you show people."}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "If someone's already seen a tip,"}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "don't repeat it in the same"}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "session."}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "And finally, to show Loading"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "progress, always favor progress"}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "bars over activity indicators"}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "because they do a much better"}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "job communicating what's"}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "happening and how long it will"}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "take."}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "So, no matter when your game"}, {"start": 151.0, "text": "needs to load, entertain,"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "educate, and show progress."}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "All right, next is Quick Start."}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "Being able to start quickly and"}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "jump into your game is key to a"}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "great game experience."}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "This is INKS, and it's an Apple"}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "Design Award winner from last"}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "year."}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "It's really fun that you're able"}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "to get a feeling for the game"}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "right from launch, but also they"}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "do a great job making it obvious"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "on how to start the game with"}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "this large turquoise Play"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "button."}, {"start": 180.0, "text": "And as soon as you tap it, there"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "are only two screens before"}, {"start": 183.0, "text": "you're in and playing the game,"}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "which is awesome."}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "So, let people get into your"}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "game easily and quickly."}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "Don't ask players to make too"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "many choices before they"}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "understand what it means in your"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "game."}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "And for more complex games, I"}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "know there are important things"}, {"start": 199.0, "text": "that you want to show your"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "players."}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "And game Main Menus have become"}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "increasingly busy with news,"}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "tournaments, stores, and more."}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "And these can all be on your"}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "interface, but make sure that"}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "the main call to action to play,"}, {"start": 215.0, "text": "start, battle, or begin a new"}, {"start": 217.0, "text": "game is the most dominant in"}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "your Main Menu UI."}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "All right, tip 4 is all about"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "our game's interface, and before"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "we jump into this tip, you"}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "should know something about me,"}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "and that's, I have a soft spot"}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "for classic arcade games."}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "So, this fake alien monster game"}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "is going to help us with a few"}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "user interface best practices,"}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "starting with consistency."}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "Consistency improves usability"}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "because it helps people mentally"}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "map your interface."}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "It's much easier to play and"}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "navigate when controls are in"}, {"start": 253.0, "text": "predictable locations."}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "So, be consistent in the layout"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "of your game's menu."}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "That way, people can spend their"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "energy playing your game versus"}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "trying to recall where was that"}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "Settings button."}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "So, let's look at this exact"}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "same flow with an inconsistent"}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "UI."}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "The Back button is all over the"}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "place, and Settings disappears"}, {"start": 274.0, "text": "on the Choose Character screen."}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "This inconsistency disrupts a"}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "player's experience because it"}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "takes more effort to mentally"}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "map the interface."}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "So, when you're designing, to"}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "accommodate for consistency, lay"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "out all of your screens and"}, {"start": 289.0, "text": "check them."}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "That way, you'll be able to tell"}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "whether the controls are in the"}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "same place."}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "Okay. The next UI best practice"}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "is all about clarity."}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "It needs to be clear to players"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "what's interactive and what's"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "not. If people have to think too much"}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "about what to tap, they're going"}, {"start": 305.0, "text": "to be taken out of your game's"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "experience."}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "So, items that are tappable need"}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "to look different from items"}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "that are not tappable."}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "So, in the top center of this"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "screen, my Lives is actually"}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "just status, but with this"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "visual appearance, it could be"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "confused for something that's"}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "interactive."}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "This is common in a lot of"}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "games, and there is an easy fix."}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "Make non-interactive elements"}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "look different by using color"}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "and shape, like this or this."}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "Or you can remove and put status"}, {"start": 334.0, "text": "items away from interactive"}, {"start": 336.0, "text": "elements."}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "In your interface, for clarity,"}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "it's important always to include"}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "three visual states for buttons"}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "and controls because a lack of"}, {"start": 346.0, "text": "visual feedback can confuse"}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "players."}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "Be sure to use a Normal state to"}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "show people that something's"}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "tappable."}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "Use a Press state when something"}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "has been tapped."}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "And finally, use a Disabled"}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "state for control that's not"}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "currently active or enabled."}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "Many developers struggle if they"}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "should remove or hide a control"}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "if it cannot be activated, but"}, {"start": 368.0, "text": "if you do that, when it does pop"}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "back it could be really"}, {"start": 371.0, "text": "confusing to players, especially"}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "if this happens during gameplay."}, {"start": 376.0, "text": "So, for a much better user"}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "experience, use a Disabled"}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "state."}, {"start": 380.0, "text": "This lets people know the"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "control's location and action"}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "that will be possible soon when"}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "that control is enabled."}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "And finally, make sure that"}, {"start": 388.0, "text": "everything that's interactive on"}, {"start": 390.0, "text": "your game's interface meets the"}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "minimum tap targets on iOS which"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "is 44 by 44 points."}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "Your interface is a tool to make"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "sense of your game's world, so"}, {"start": 401.0, "text": "make it consistent and clear."}, {"start": 403.0, "text": "That way, people will be able to"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "stay engaged in your game."}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "All right, I hope you all enjoy"}, {"start": 408.0, "text": "that fake alien monster game."}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "It'll come back in a bit to help"}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "us with a few other design tips."}, {"start": 414.0, "text": "We're already halfway through at"}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "number 5."}, {"start": 418.0, "text": "This tip and the next few are"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "about game tutorials."}, {"start": 421.0, "text": "Successful tutorials teach"}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "gradually and in context through"}, {"start": 424.0, "text": "progressive disclosure."}, {"start": 427.0, "text": "Your tutorial should be made up"}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "of three basic parts that align"}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "to the core loop of your game."}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "For example, it might be that"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "you have to fight monsters to"}, {"start": 436.0, "text": "get some gold, and then buy some"}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "stuff to fight more challenging"}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "monsters."}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "But be sure, in your tutorial,"}, {"start": 444.0, "text": "it stays to those three basic"}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "parts."}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "If you have to keep, if you have"}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "to teach about economy in your"}, {"start": 451.0, "text": "game, keep it simple because"}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "remember you're teaching"}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "somebody something brand new."}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "So, avoid overwhelming people"}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "and including information in"}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "your tutorial that is not"}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "essential to gameplay."}, {"start": 464.0, "text": "All of this, such as upgrades,"}, {"start": 467.0, "text": "tournaments, messages, and your"}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "store can all be discovered"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "after your tutorial."}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "And also, in your tutorial it's"}, {"start": 475.0, "text": "really important to provide"}, {"start": 476.0, "text": "clear direction."}, {"start": 478.0, "text": "If you have characters in your"}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "game, it's pretty common to have"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "a character walk you through the"}, {"start": 483.0, "text": "tutorial."}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "So, let's say we have this"}, {"start": 486.0, "text": "adorable alien monster, keep"}, {"start": 489.0, "text": "directions short and simple to"}, {"start": 491.0, "text": "be effective."}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "So, whether you teach with a"}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "character or through in-game"}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "instructional text, a single"}, {"start": 498.0, "text": "clear direction is going to be"}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "the most effective."}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "And please, don't repeat"}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "directions."}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "Respect your players and treat,"}, {"start": 506.0, "text": "and don't treat them like"}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "children."}, {"start": 509.0, "text": "Even if your players are"}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "children, kids are smart."}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "So, repeating directions"}, {"start": 514.0, "text": "unnecessarily lengthens your"}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "tutorial, and that makes it less"}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "effective and less fun."}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "And learning is really fun,"}, {"start": 522.0, "text": "especially when the teacher is"}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "engaging, creative, and"}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "inventive."}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "So, be the cool teacher."}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "Don't just do what you've seen"}, {"start": 530.0, "text": "others do."}, {"start": 531.0, "text": "If your game is unique, your"}, {"start": 533.0, "text": "tutorial should be too."}, {"start": 535.0, "text": "For example, think about how you"}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "can teach before your game"}, {"start": 538.0, "text": "begins."}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "This is Splitter Critters, and"}, {"start": 542.0, "text": "in this game you split the world"}, {"start": 544.0, "text": "with a swipe of your finger and"}, {"start": 546.0, "text": "then rearrange it to guide"}, {"start": 547.0, "text": "critters back to their"}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "spaceship."}, {"start": 549.0, "text": "And from the Start screen,"}, {"start": 550.0, "text": "you're taught this key game"}, {"start": 552.0, "text": "mechanic."}, {"start": 553.0, "text": "And one of the least effective"}, {"start": 555.0, "text": "ways to teach is with a bouncing"}, {"start": 557.0, "text": "arrow."}, {"start": 558.0, "text": "It's not effective because"}, {"start": 561.0, "text": "people just end up playing tap"}, {"start": 562.0, "text": "the pointing arrow game and not"}, {"start": 564.0, "text": "learning."}, {"start": 565.0, "text": "And the same goes for the"}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "floating hand."}, {"start": 568.0, "text": "Not only do you not learn, but"}, {"start": 570.0, "text": "this method is really"}, {"start": 571.0, "text": "problematic because it hides you"}, {"start": 572.0, "text": "from the interface that you're"}, {"start": 573.0, "text": "trying to be learning about."}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "So, there are much better"}, {"start": 577.0, "text": "attention-getting devices that"}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "are way more natural and"}, {"start": 580.0, "text": "immersive, such as animation."}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "This is Reigns, and I was really"}, {"start": 586.0, "text": "excited to hear that the"}, {"start": 587.0, "text": "developer is soon updating to"}, {"start": 589.0, "text": "remove the floating hand."}, {"start": 591.0, "text": "On the right, is the new"}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "experience and, as you can see,"}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "it's much more immersive; it's"}, {"start": 597.0, "text": "just as effective, and it does a"}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "great job getting you right into"}, {"start": 600.0, "text": "the world of Reigns."}, {"start": 602.0, "text": "And being in the world of your"}, {"start": 604.0, "text": "game is the best."}, {"start": 606.0, "text": "So, if you can let people jump"}, {"start": 608.0, "text": "right in and learn through play,"}, {"start": 610.0, "text": "that is going to be the most"}, {"start": 612.0, "text": "effective way to teach them your"}, {"start": 614.0, "text": "game."}, {"start": 615.0, "text": "So, this is Mars: Mars on Apple"}, {"start": 618.0, "text": "TV."}, {"start": 619.0, "text": "And it is really fun to be able"}, {"start": 620.0, "text": "to jump right into the game."}, {"start": 623.0, "text": "So right now, I'm on Mars, and"}, {"start": 624.0, "text": "the controls are intuitive, so"}, {"start": 626.0, "text": "I'm going to start clicking around."}, {"start": 627.0, "text": "And after one hilarious death, I"}, {"start": 631.0, "text": "quickly realize that the"}, {"start": 632.0, "text": "objective is to land safely on"}, {"start": 634.0, "text": "the stations."}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "So, for the best experience,"}, {"start": 638.0, "text": "teach people through play."}, {"start": 641.0, "text": "All right, we're already at"}, {"start": 644.0, "text": "number 9, which is all about"}, {"start": 647.0, "text": "letting people skip and get"}, {"start": 648.0, "text": "right into your game."}, {"start": 651.0, "text": "Give the player control, and"}, {"start": 652.0, "text": "that way Skip can create a much"}, {"start": 654.0, "text": "better user experience."}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "Now, I love this opening"}, {"start": 659.0, "text": "sequence from Icycle: On Thin"}, {"start": 661.0, "text": "Ice. It's clever, has a striking"}, {"start": 663.0, "text": "style, and it provides you with"}, {"start": 665.0, "text": "the motivation of the main"}, {"start": 666.0, "text": "character, Dennis."}, {"start": 668.0, "text": "But when you tap on the screen,"}, {"start": 669.0, "text": "a very subtle Skip button"}, {"start": 671.0, "text": "appears."}, {"start": 672.0, "text": "And that is great because"}, {"start": 674.0, "text": "revealing Skip on tap is a"}, {"start": 676.0, "text": "wonderful technique."}, {"start": 678.0, "text": "Players who are ready to jump"}, {"start": 680.0, "text": "right into your game can, and"}, {"start": 682.0, "text": "people who want to watch the"}, {"start": 683.0, "text": "entire sequence can stay"}, {"start": 684.0, "text": "immersed with edge to edge"}, {"start": 685.0, "text": "playback."}, {"start": 687.0, "text": "Now, letting players Skip also"}, {"start": 689.0, "text": "applies to tutorials."}, {"start": 692.0, "text": "This is Zombie Gunship, and"}, {"start": 694.0, "text": "check out the upper left-hand"}, {"start": 696.0, "text": "corner. It's awesome."}, {"start": 697.0, "text": "There is a Skip Tutorial button,"}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "and it feels great to be able to"}, {"start": 701.0, "text": "jump right into the game."}, {"start": 703.0, "text": "Just be sure if you allow people"}, {"start": 705.0, "text": "to Skip your tutorial, they're"}, {"start": 707.0, "text": "able to relaunch or replay the"}, {"start": 709.0, "text": "tutorial in case they need a"}, {"start": 710.0, "text": "refresher on the rules."}, {"start": 712.0, "text": "Now, I understand that this may"}, {"start": 714.0, "text": "not work for every game."}, {"start": 716.0, "text": "So, if it's critical to your"}, {"start": 717.0, "text": "game's progression to include a"}, {"start": 719.0, "text": "tutorial level, teach the"}, {"start": 721.0, "text": "basics, gradually adding context"}, {"start": 723.0, "text": "through progressive disclosure,"}, {"start": 725.0, "text": "and then get out of the way."}, {"start": 728.0, "text": "Letting players Skip is about"}, {"start": 730.0, "text": "putting the player's experience"}, {"start": 732.0, "text": "first because you don't know"}, {"start": 734.0, "text": "someone's skill level or how"}, {"start": 737.0, "text": "much time they have to play your"}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "game."}, {"start": 739.0, "text": "And I'm sure we have all button"}, {"start": 742.0, "text": "smashed and clicked as quickly"}, {"start": 744.0, "text": "as possible to get through a"}, {"start": 745.0, "text": "tutorial just to get into the"}, {"start": 746.0, "text": "game."}, {"start": 747.0, "text": "So, for a much better user"}, {"start": 749.0, "text": "experience, provide a Skip"}, {"start": 751.0, "text": "Tutorial button."}, {"start": 753.0, "text": "So, respect the player and that"}, {"start": 756.0, "text": "way, they will be able to have a"}, {"start": 758.0, "text": "much better user experience."}, {"start": 761.0, "text": "The final design tip today is"}, {"start": 763.0, "text": "about being inclusive."}, {"start": 766.0, "text": "There's a lot that you can do to"}, {"start": 768.0, "text": "make your game more accessible,"}, {"start": 770.0, "text": "such as adding Closed Captions"}, {"start": 772.0, "text": "or supporting Dynamic Type."}, {"start": 774.0, "text": "You can also, just like in"}, {"start": 776.0, "text": "Mushroom 11, support Left and"}, {"start": 779.0, "text": "Right-Hand Mode, or you can"}, {"start": 782.0, "text": "support Color Blind Mode, like"}, {"start": 783.0, "text": "in KAMI 2."}, {"start": 785.0, "text": "And one of the coolest"}, {"start": 786.0, "text": "Accessibility updates that I"}, {"start": 787.0, "text": "have seen is from Blackbox,"}, {"start": 790.0, "text": "which is a visual puzzler that"}, {"start": 792.0, "text": "now includes sonic interfaces to"}, {"start": 794.0, "text": "let players with low or no"}, {"start": 795.0, "text": "vision play through solving"}, {"start": 797.0, "text": "puzzles with sound."}, {"start": 799.0, "text": "With 285 million blind or"}, {"start": 801.0, "text": "low-vision people in the world,"}, {"start": 803.0, "text": "everybody should be able to play"}, {"start": 805.0, "text": "games and have fun."}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "All right, with these 10 design"}, {"start": 810.0, "text": "tips, you'll be able to create"}, {"start": 811.0, "text": "great experiences from the"}, {"start": 813.0, "text": "moment someone taps your icon."}, {"start": 816.0, "text": "But remember, of all things,"}, {"start": 818.0, "text": "respect your players, include"}, {"start": 820.0, "text": "everyone, and put their"}, {"start": 822.0, "text": "experience first."}]}
